## HEAVY
At most TWO heavy jobs run machine-wide across MPS lanes. A heavy job = `npm ci`, a whole `npx vitest run`, `npm run build`, `npx tsc -b`, `npx eslint .` over the whole web folder, a CodeQL database create or analyse, or any dotnet build or test. A single-file `npx vitest run <file>` is light, as are `git`, `gh` reads and a single-file edit. Take a slot by atomic `mkdir '<project>/.tools/.heavy-lock-1'` (else `-2`; neither free: poll every 60 s), write `holder.txt` (pane name, label, `date`), run ONE job, release by MOVING the holder file to `.tools/b1641/logs/` and `rmdir` your own dir. **Load gate: `LC_ALL=C uptime` load1 under 24 on TWO reads 120 s apart (not independent: say so)** (the product owner's 2026-11-11 ruling for this 18-CPU machine). A holder older than 30 minutes with no live pane is REPORTED, never removed. A wait is not a finding; waited 60 minutes: say so; at the hard stop `BLOCKED: heavy lock waiting at load <n>`. The drafter's own whole-suite runs took about 20 seconds each here (UNMEASURED under the lock protocol; the drafter took no lock and load was 8 to 11).

